---
// "Live in Claude Code" band: screenshots of the mod panels (map panel, pipeline band, burn-down).
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import mapPanel from "../../assets/screenshots/map-panel.png";
import workStateBand from "../../assets/screenshots/work-state-band.png";
import burndown from "../../assets/screenshots/burndown.png";
---

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Live in Claude Code</span>
    <h2 class="h2">The map stays on screen while you work</h2>
    <p class="sub">In Claude Code the trailhead mod draws the work beside the conversation: the active map's tickets, the step you're on, and how the map is burning down.</p>
    <div class="shots">
      <figure class="shot wide">
        <Image src={mapPanel} alt="The trailhead map panel docked beside the Claude Code transcript: the open maps, the frontier with a work button per ticket, tickets in progress and blocked, and a footer with refresh and close" />
        <figcaption><span class="vcmd"><span class="s">/trailhead:</span>panel</span>The <b>map panel</b>: every open map to view, the frontier with a <b>work</b> button per ticket, who holds what, and what is blocked.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot">
        <Image src={workStateBand} alt="The pipeline band above the prompt showing the ticket in play and its discuss, plan, execute, verify steps, with the trailhead status entry below" />
        <figcaption>The <b>pipeline band</b> and <b>status entry</b>: the ticket in play and the step it's on: the band above the prompt, the status entry under it.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot">
        <Image src={burndown} alt="The burn-down section of the map panel: open, done, removed and peak counts over a chart of open tickets from the map's first ticket to now" />
        <figcaption>The <b>burn-down</b>: open tickets over time, from the map's first ticket to now.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="shots-note">Claude Code 2.1.287+ · ships inside the trailhead plugin · Codex keeps the command hooks</p>
  </div>
</section>
